.TH CHM-REBOOT 1
.SH NAME
chm-reboot \\- manage a user-approved Chimera II OS reboot request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chm-reboot
.RI [ status | now | later | cancel ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports and manages reboot requests created by staged system patches. A patch that requires reboot records a pending request and does not reboot silently.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the pending reboot reason and artifact.
.TP
.B now
Record that the user approved reboot. Actual platform reboot remains under Koronos/Aegis policy.
.TP
.B later
Defer the reboot while keeping the request pending.
.TP
.B cancel
Clear the pending request.
